      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1907 the name changed to Fremont, honoring explorer John C. Frémont, though some maps still called it Peggy for years afterward.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fremont%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1917 iron smelter built near Pike Creek sparked the creation of the nearby community of Midco, just two miles north of Fremont.",
